  {q:"What is the significance of the International Court of Justice for resolving border disputes?",correct:"The ICJ provides a legal forum for countries to resolve territorial disputes peacefully, though its decisions lack enforcement mechanisms against unwilling states",options:["The ICJ has a military force","The ICJ provides a legal forum for countries to resolve territorial disputes peacefully, though its decisions lack enforcement mechanisms against unwilling states","All countries accept ICJ rulings","The ICJ only handles human rights cases"],fact:"Nicaragua vs. Colombia over maritime boundaries is one of the ICJ's most important cases — redefining Caribbean borders between the two countries, though enforcing the ruling required further diplomatic pressure!"},
  {q:"What is the relationship between diaspora communities and national flag symbolism?",correct:"Diaspora communities often maintain deep attachment to homeland flags as identity markers — and sometimes maintain political connections that influence foreign policy",options:["Diaspora communities abandon homeland symbols","Diaspora communities often maintain deep attachment to homeland flags as identity markers — and sometimes maintain political connections that influence foreign policy","Flags lose meaning outside the homeland","Diaspora politics are irrelevant to international relations"],fact:"The Irish-American diaspora's political support for Irish nationalism shaped US policy toward the British-Irish conflict for over a century — diaspora communities can be more nationalist than homeland populations!"},
  {q:"What makes the flag of Brazil unique among national flags?",correct:"It features an astronomical sky map showing the night sky over Rio de Janeiro on the exact date (November 15, 1889) the Republic was proclaimed",options:["It has the most colors","It's the largest flag by design","It features an astronomical sky map showing the night sky over Rio de Janeiro on the exact date (November 15, 1889) the Republic was proclaimed","It was designed by a famous artist"],fact:"Each Brazilian state has a corresponding star on the flag. The constellation positions are astronomically accurate for 8:30 PM on November 15, 1889 — making it one of the most scientifically precise national flags!"}
